## Context
DESIGN-V2 §2.8 gates, honoring R19-R21, R26/R27, and v1's Risk-3 soak — repo-
side work in this repo's Makefile and bench/, not upstream PRs. Target shape:
`check: lint figures fold-gate golden check-fast`; `check-slow: check rss-gate
convergence soak`.
- R19 fold gate: fold_sweep.mjs repointed at the tree under test; against
  stock upstream it is red BY CLASSIFICATION (recorded miss count), not by
  crash; waiver keyed to PR #19's URL, deleted on merge (0014).
- R21 golden gate, D11=set: pinned multilingual fixture corpus, ~40 queries,
  answer sets at k=10. Thresholds re-derived after the operator critique's F1
  kill (0013's legitimate minimum is 0.25, not above 0.5): mean Jaccard >=
  0.8; <= 5% of queries below 0.35; hard floor 0.2. Order deliberately
  ungated. Re-pins are commits whose set diff is the review artifact; re-pin
  at entry granularity when entries exist.
- R20 RSS gate: deterministic synthetic monster at 44,906,152 chars, entry-
  structured (~43k headings); assert worker VmHWM <= 500 MB, server p95 <=
  300 MB. Fixture informed by X3 (0025).
- R26/R27 convergence harness: fixture library, empty dataDir, 1 Hz status
  polls touching nothing else; asserts status <= 50 ms, monotone coverage,
  prefix arithmetic per stage at DESIGN-V2 §2.3's granularities; then
  edit-one-count-one and the identical-bytes resync with all work deltas 0 —
  the test that would have caught the shipped 92.7% defect. Phase 3 fixture:
  one quarantine, one monster, dateAdded ties.
- R13 soak: three P0s, full 10k drain, 1 query/s each, kill -9 the conductor
  twice; p95 <= 1.5 s, zero SQLITE_BUSY surfacing, WAL <= 256 MB, lease
  migration < 30 s, zero double-commits.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] fold gate in `make check`, red-by-classification against stock upstream, waiver documented
- [ ] golden gate with the re-derived thresholds and a committed pinned set
- [ ] rss gate asserting the ratified budgets against the synthetic monster
- [ ] convergence harness phases 1-3 runnable; resync phase asserts zero work
- [ ] soak scripted with the five assertions; results committed to bench/results/
